#
# Title labels for https://github.com/github/issue-labeler (v3.5), applied to
# pull-request titles by .github/workflows/pr_labeler.yml and to issue titles
# by .github/workflows/issue_labeler.yml.
#
# Source of truth: [tool.scikitplot.maintenance.labeler.title_prefixes] and
# title_keywords in pyproject.toml. One prefix gives exactly one label.
#
# Prefix rules match the start of the title, case-insensitively: an optional
# "[", a list of known prefixes joined by ",", "/" or "+", then an explicit
# terminator - "]" (optionally ":"), "(scope):" or ":":
#   "BUG: ...", "[Bug]: ...", "[BUG] ...", "BUG, TST: ...", "MAINT(ci): ..."
# Without a terminator nothing matches: "Fix typo", "Bug in reader" and
# "DOCKER image" get no prefix label. Keyword rules match whole words anywhere.
#
# Edit the template (tools/maint_tools/templates/labeler-issue.yml.in) or the
# policy, then regenerate and check:
#   python tools/maint_tools/generate_pr_labeler.py sync --apply
#   python tools/maint_tools/generate_pr_labeler.py check
